# Engineering-owned shared configuration is published to GitHub Packages, not
# npmjs.com, so the @jrmoulckers scope needs an explicit registry.
# See https://github.com/jrmoulckers/engineering/blob/main/docs/adopting.md
@jrmoulckers:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com

# No credential is committed here. `docs/adopting.md` shows
# `//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}` on this line, but pnpm
# deliberately refuses to expand environment variables in credentials that come
# from a project-level .npmrc, so the line would only emit a warning on every
# install. Supply the token out of band instead:
#   local  - pnpm config set "//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken" <read:packages PAT> --location=user
#   CI     - actions/setup-node with registry-url + scope, and NODE_AUTH_TOKEN in env
